Backport: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/commit/d1175e88b46b80d5375522e7ea7977544e20fe6b
Upstream PR #140593 (v2026.9.3): fix(windows): avoid compiler-triggered gateway startup failures.

v2026.8.1 creates private Windows SQLite staging directories by spawning
PowerShell with an Add-Type compiler step. Security software or policy that
refuses `LobsterAI.exe -> powershell.exe` (CreateProcess ACCESS_DENIED, which
Node reports as `spawn EPERM`) then breaks legacy session import, device
identity migration, the Gateway write-admission preflight and Doctor itself.
Create the directory through Koffi and the Win32 security APIs instead, keeping
the atomic protected DACL and exclusive creation.

LobsterAI addition: when the native helper cannot load (stubbed Koffi or a
blocked addon), roots inside %USERPROFILE% fall back to exclusive mkdir with the
inherited owner/SYSTEM/Administrators ACL; every other root stays fail-closed.
The upstream commit's update-cli restart-helper changes are not needed here.
Windows runtimes must ship the real koffi package (see prune-openclaw-runtime).
Retire when the pinned upstream reaches v2026.9.3.

